OL,4,CClip of long-lost early children's TV  
OL,5,Cshow found                             
OL,6,GA chance find on an audio cassette has 
OL,7,Gled to the recovery of the only known  
OL,8,Gsurviving material from one of         
OL,9,GBritain's first popular children's     
OL,10,Gtelevision shows.                      
OL,12,FWhirligig ran for more than 90         
OL,13,Fepisodes from 1950 to 1956, but no     
OL,14,Frecordings from the series were        
OL,15,Fthought to exist.                      
OL,17,FThe find was made by Stuart Woodhead   
OL,18,Ffrom Grimsby, who runs the Joy Laurey  
OL,19,FArchive, which is dedicated to one of  
OL,20,FWhirligig's resident puppeteers.       
OL,22,                                   G4/4 
